Usage: cloud-firestore-emulator [options] <ignored>
  Options:
    --database-mode
      Cloud Firestore database mode supports `firestore-native` and 
      `datastore-mode` 
      Default: CLOUD_FIRESTORE
      Possible Values: [CLOUD_DATASTORE, CLOUD_FIRESTORE_IN_DATASTORE_MODE, CLOUD_FIRESTORE]
    --export-name
      Export name for emulator export (e.g., 
      ../exportName.overall_export_metadata). 
    --export-on-exit
      Directory path for emulator export.
    --functions_emulator
      The HTTP host and port of the Functions Emulator. (e.g. localhost:9002)
    --help
      Print usage and exit
    --host
      The address to bind to on the local machine
      Default: localhost
    --import-data
      File path to data being imported into the emulator.
    --licenses
      Print open-source dependencies and licenses, then exit
      Default: false
    --port
      The port number to listen to on the local machine
      Default: 8080
    --project_id
      Project ID to be used for single project mode
    --rules
      Cloud Firestore rules file
    --seed_from_export
      Local filesystem path to a Cloud Firestore export (e.g., 
      '/home/foo/firestore_export/2019-10-22T19:41:32_89121.overall_export_metadata') 
    --single_project_mode
      Whether to operate in single project mode. If set, warnings will be 
      logged for project ID not matching the provided project_id flag.
      Default: false
    --single_project_mode_error
      Turns project ID mismatches from warnings to errors.
      Default: false
    --version
      Print version and exit
      Default: false
    --webchannel_port
      The port number to bind for WebChannel traffic
    --websocket_port
      The port number for the emulator ui

